  "description": "The palmar forearm and wrist. At the wrist the palmaris longus and flexor carpi radialis tendons are superficial; the median nerve lies just deep to and between them and runs up the middle of the forearm under the superficial flexors. The radial artery lies lateral to flexor carpi radialis; on the ulnar side the ulnar artery and nerve run radial to flexor carpi ulnaris. Over the distal radius on the radial aspect the bone is close under the skin and tendons, with the cephalic vein and the superficial branch of the radial nerve in the subcutaneous tissue.",
